## Context

Intro paragraph 4 ends (`slides/manuscript/main.tex:158–162`):

> The benchmark earns its keep by being usable without the gold
> reference: reference-free coherence criteria suffice to screen out the
> weakest runs and the weakest models, so the cheap part of the quality
> score can stand in for the expensive part when triaging which outputs
> deserve human attention.

Two fixes:
1. **Drop the "The benchmark earns its keep by being usable without the
   gold reference:" clause** at the start. The real subject is the
   existing correlation and its consequence — not the benchmark
   congratulating itself. Recast so the sentence leads with the finding:
   that reference-free coherence criteria track accuracy, and therefore
   screen the weakest runs and models without the gold reference.
   (Suggested: "Reference-free coherence criteria suffice to screen out
   the weakest runs and the weakest models, so the cheap part of the
   quality score can stand in for the expensive part when triaging which
   outputs deserve attention.")
2. **Delete "human"** before "attention" → "deserve attention".

Note the dependency on [[0598]]: that ticket drops the ρ regression and
makes the screening point via `fig:reliability`. Keep this sentence's
claim consistent with 0598 — the screening conclusion stays, the
correlation coefficient does not.

